(929630, 107983, 6349, '<td valign="top">My pick for the yellow ribbon.  Congrats on an excellent image.  Good luck in the challenge.  10</td>', 'My pick for the yellow ribbon.  Congrats on an excellent image.  Good luck in the challenge.  10', '2004-09-28 20:24:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(929633, 108006, 5792, '<td valign="top">Soft focus definitely hurts this image. Something like this should be in razor sharp focus. Though it fits the challenge topic creativity is also an issue here. For some reason circuit boards and hard drives are common photo subjects at DPC and are overdone, sorta like the desaturation to one color technique is also overworked.</td>', 'Soft focus definitely hurts this image. Something like this should be in razor sharp focus. Though it fits the challenge topic creativity is also an issue here. For some reason circuit boards and hard drives are common photo subjects at DPC and are overdone, sorta like the desaturation to one color technique is also overworked.', '2004-09-28 20:25:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(929635, 106818, 6349, '<td valign="top">In my opinion this may be the best image in terms of fitting the challenge.  Your subject(s) are complex yet the photograph itself is far more complex.  I couldn''t image 3 more contradicting shapes working so well together.  Good luck in the challenge.  10</td>', 'In my opinion this may be the best image in terms of fitting the challenge.  Your subject(s) are complex yet the photograph itself is far more complex.  I couldn''t image 3 more contradicting shapes working so well together.  Good luck in the challenge.  10', '2004-09-28 20:27:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(929636, 107973, 6349, '<td valign="top">I think this will ribbon.  Great work.  I''m curious to know if that is the natural color of the light?  All similar shots I have seen have been more golden.  10</td>', 'I think this will ribbon.  Great work.  I''m curious to know if that is the natural color of the light?  All similar shots I have seen have been more golden.  10', '2004-09-28 20:27:57.000000', NULL, 1),
