(940689, 106529, 8367, '<td valign="top">Very, very creative. Great job!  (I wish I had your eyelashes. :D )</td>', 'Very, very creative. Great job!  (I wish I had your eyelashes. :D )', '2004-10-04 13:01:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(940699, 107893, 13381, '<td valign="top">I think this is a very interesting shot visually -- and I actually like the crop better than I liked the crop of the original. It sort of resembles a keyhole -- very interesting in its asymmetry. Great job. :)</td>', 'I think this is a very interesting shot visually -- and I actually like the crop better than I liked the crop of the original. It sort of resembles a keyhole -- very interesting in its asymmetry. Great job. :)', '2004-10-04 13:07:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(940709, 107620, 11467, '<td valign="top">I agree with Siggi.<br/>A lot of work, and an interesting picture as a result.</td>', 'I agree with Siggi.A lot of work, and an interesting picture as a result.', '2004-10-04 13:14:12.000000', NULL, 0),
(940726, 107973, 5792, '<td valign="top">Thanks to all for your very kind comments and generous scores. Now if I could just figure a way to get a blue one... :)<br/> <br/>Slot canyons are fascinating and sometimes dangerous places to photograph.<br/> <br/>A couple miles from this location is Lower Antelope Slot Canyon. 11 people on a tour got trapped and drowned during a flash flood there in 1997. Where I took this picture I was told that the week before a flash flood came through and raised the floor level by 5 to 6 feet! Both events are unusual, but do happen.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-10-04 12:24:57.</i></td>', 'Thanks to all for your very kind comments and generous scores. Now if I could just figure a way to get a blue one... :) Slot canyons are fascinating and sometimes dangerous places to photograph. A couple miles from this location is Lower Antelope Slot Canyon. 11 people on a tour got trapped and drowned during a flash flood there in 1997. Where I took this picture I was told that the week before a flash flood came through and raised the floor level by 5 to 6 feet! Both events are unusual, but do happen.', '2004-10-04 13:23:22.000000', '2004-10-04 13:24:57.000000', 0),
(940734, 107973, 27524, '<td valign="top">Great! :) I was sure you should get something for this...</td>', 'Great! :) I was sure you should get something for this...', '2004-10-04 13:28:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(940741, 107893, 27524, '<td valign="top">Good but i hopet it will get bit higher...pitty :) cuz it was my favorite.</td>', 'Good but i hopet it will get bit higher...pitty :) cuz it was my favorite.', '2004-10-04 13:32:05.000000', NULL, 0),
(940775, 107747, 24495, '<td valign="top">Excellent Night Shot! Can I take a printout, with permission!</td>', 'Excellent Night Shot! Can I take a printout, with permission!', '2004-10-04 13:48:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(940791, 108101, 27524, '<td valign="top">:) That was close... 5th...congrats.</td>', ':) That was close... 5th...congrats.', '2004-10-04 13:55:13.000000', NULL, 0),
(940792, 106529, 1031, '<td valign="top">I find it fascinating that no one has commented on your two-toned border.<br/> <br/>Are you going to explain the set-up for this? (Even if it''s the "hard" way -- I guess you can keep the secret shortcut to yourself for a while.)</td>', 'I find it fascinating that no one has commented on your two-toned border. Are you going to explain the set-up for this? (Even if it''s the "hard" way -- I guess you can keep the secret shortcut to yourself for a while.)', '2004-10-04 13:55:57.000000', NULL, 0),
(940826, 107895, 21317, '<td valign="top">For those who asked about the technique, It is a flag under a suspended glass with water drops on it (the glass is treated with RainX). There was a tutorial on how to do this by John Seltzer -Jmseltzer- (who I believe introduced the technique to DPC) but I cannot find it now, it is a shame, it was great!!!. <br/> <br/>For those who asked about the subject, xtabintun was right, it is the Venezuelan flag.<br/> <br/>Alex<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-01-26 00:10:07.</i></td>', 'For those who asked about the technique, It is a flag under a suspended glass with water drops on it (the glass is treated with RainX). There was a tutorial on how to do this by John Seltzer -Jmseltzer- (who I believe introduced the technique to DPC) but I cannot find it now, it is a shame, it was great!!!.  For those who asked about the subject, xtabintun was right, it is the Venezuelan flag. Alex', '2004-10-04 14:06:35.000000', '2006-01-26 00:10:07.000000', 0),
